5. Performance (CPU): JAX driver vs. real Fortran per-routine cost
======================================================================
  JAX (this CPU, jit-compiled, 20-step average): 33.51 ms/DTsrc-step

  Real Fortran per-routine cost, measured in P2SAoM40.PRT (194 real
  DTsrc steps, single MPI process, same CPU-class hardware):
    RADIA()            65.57% of runtime, avg 2070 ms/call
                        (bimodal: ~0.7ms on 4/5 steps, ~10833ms on the
                         NRAD=5-gated 1/5 steps -- real spectral
                         radiative transfer; JAX's radiation_jax.py is
                         a simplified graybody formula, so this huge
                         JAX/Fortran gap reflects a fidelity difference,
                         not an apples-to-apples speed comparison)
    SURFACE()           8.87% of runtime, avg  263 ms/call
                        (includes NIsurf=2 PBL+EARTH+layer-1 substeps)
    GROUND_SI/LI/LK    ~0.16% of runtime, avg    ~1 ms/call combined
    ---- JAX-covered subset: ~74.6% of real per-step Fortran cost ----
    CONDSE() (moist convection)  9.91% -- OUT OF SCOPE, not ported
    Atm. Dynamics                8.50% -- OUT OF SCOPE, not ported

